---
import Layout from "../layout.astro";

---
<Layout title="RIPL Portfolios | RIPL Wealth" description="Give every dollar a job with RIPL Portfolios. Organize money for Today, Tomorrow and Beyond around your goals and when you need it.">
<section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">RIPL PORTFOLIOS</div><h1>Every dollar<br><span class="ripl-gold">gets a job.</span></h1><p class="lead">Start with when you need the money and what it needs to do.</p><div class="page-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Talk to the Team</a><a class="text-link" href="#three-rings">Explore the three rings ↓</a></div></div></section>


<section class="section dark"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Time. Purpose.<br>Structure.</h2><div><p class="lead">“Risk is not volatility. Risk is your money not being ready when you are.”</p><p class="small">That is our planning lens. Market losses, inflation, access to your money and the strength of an issuer still matter. No investment approach removes every risk.</p><p>Near-term spending and long-term growth have different jobs. Treating them the same can leave you selling at the wrong time or keeping too much money on the sidelines.</p><p>We organize your money around your timelines and goals. Your plan gives the portfolio its purpose.</p></div></div></section>


<section class="section" id="three-rings"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">THE THREE RINGS</div><h2>When you build around your timeline instead of the market’s, everything shifts.</h2>
  <div class="rings">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 400 400" role="img" aria-label="Three rings around a center point. The inner ring is Today, the middle ring is Tomorrow, the outer ring is Beyond.">
      <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="188" fill="#ECEAF4" stroke="#B8A8E8" stroke-width="1.5"></circle>
      <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="130" fill="#D9D3F0" stroke="#8E80D0" stroke-width="1.5"></circle>
      <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="72" fill="#6355B8" stroke="#6355B8" stroke-width="1.5"></circle>
      <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="7" fill="#C9963A"></circle>
      <g font-family="Rokkitt, Georgia, serif" font-weight="600" font-size="21" text-anchor="middle">
        <text x="200" y="174" fill="#FFFFFF">Today</text>
        <text x="200" y="106" fill="#130F2A">Tomorrow</text>
        <text x="200" y="48" fill="#130F2A">Beyond</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <div class="ring-list">
      <div><span class="num">0 TO 1 YEAR</span><h3>Today</h3><p>Money you may need in the next year. The focus is keeping it available and protecting its value, with attention to the risks of the account or investment used.</p><p class="ring-job"><b>Primary job:</b> Be ready when you need it.</p></div>
      <div><span class="num">1 TO 5 YEARS</span><h3>Tomorrow</h3><p>Money for the next few years. We build the structure up front with the goal of balance: growth when growth is possible, and access when access is needed.</p><p class="ring-job"><b>Primary job:</b> Grow at a measured pace.</p></div>
      <div><span class="num">5 YEARS AND BEYOND</span><h3>Beyond</h3><p>Money you will not need for a long time. It has time on its side, and it is building your investment business.</p><p class="ring-job"><b>Primary job:</b> Grow in a way that will help you reach your goal.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>





<section class="section dark"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">WHERE IT GOES WRONG</div><div class="questions-head"><h2>Two common<br>challenges we see.</h2><p>Most people who come into our office have at least one of these two common problems.</p></div>
  <div class="pillar-grid">
    <div class="pillar"><span class="num">01</span><h3>Money is set up with the wrong time frame.</h3><p>Money you need soon is sitting where it can drop. Or money you will not touch for years is sitting in cash.</p></div>
    <div class="pillar"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Money is set up with the right time frame, but it is not doing its job.</h3><p>The timing is right. What it is invested in is not built for that timing.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>




<section class="section questions" id="investment-tools"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Most portfolios have no strategy.<br>They have positions.</h2><div><p class="lead">Positions are things you own. A strategy is the reason you own them.</p><p>When all you have is positions, nothing tells you what to sell when you need money, how much cash is too much, or whether you are on track.</p><p>With a strategy, every dollar gets assigned a job, organized by when it is needed.</p><p>Some dollars keep you safe. Some create income. Some grow. Some are for giving. Some are for the next generation.</p><p>We compare the complete picture: how you can gain, how you can lose, what you give up, and when you can access your money.</p><p>We give you access to tools most investors never see and most advisors never use.</p><div class="page-actions"><a class="text-link" href="/structured-notes/">Understand Structured Notes →</a><a class="text-link" href="/money-questions/#mq-investing">Explore Investing Questions →</a></div></div></div></section>

<section class="final-cta"><div class="wrap"><h2>What does your money<br>need to do next?</h2><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Talk to the Team</a></div></section>


</Layout>
